      "writtenOn": "2021-10-01T12:43:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The standards rules on unions are fairly strict: After you write to one member of a union (the active member), that\u0027s the only member you\u0027re allowed to read from, until you write to another (and change which member is active). Essentially, using unions to do type-casting (or presumably, the kind of renaming that\u0027s happening here) is forbidden. The compiler can\u0027t really enforce that statically, but UBSAN checks for it at runtime.",
      "parentUuid": "4b3fee0f_4da06c38",
      "revId": "59e6fea9f08c1e478ac526365396b94c0f8f0d1d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a0e4df33_510eef60",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
